    "section_mhNr64": {
      "type": "section",
      "blocks": {
        "text_nm8aU4": {
          "type": "text",
          "name": "t:names.heading",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Was Kakao in Ihnen bewirkt</p>",
            "width": "fit-content",
            "max_width": "narrow",
            "alignment": "left",
            "type_preset": "h3",
            "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
            "font_size": "",
            "line_height": "normal",
            "letter_spacing": "normal",
            "case": "none",
            "wrap": "pretty",
            "text_color": "",
            "background": false,
            "background_color": "#00000026",
            "corner_radius": 0,
            "padding-block-start": 0,
            "padding-block-end": 0,
            "padding-inline-start": 0,
            "padding-inline-end": 0
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "text_y9Mfr7": {
          "type": "text",
          "name": "t:names.description",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Kakao wird von der Menschheit seit Jahrtausenden als Stimulans genutzt. Er zählt zu den Lebensmitteln mit dem höchsten Gehalt an Antioxidantien – und enthält eine Handvoll natürlich vorkommender Verbindungen, die nicht nur gut tun, sondern die Leistung steigern. Unverarbeitet, nicht alkalisiert, aus ganzen Bohnen: So bleibt davon am meisten in der Tasse.</p>",
            "width": "100%",
            "max_width": "none",
            "alignment": "left",
            "type_preset": "rte",
            "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
            "font_size": "1rem",
            "line_height": "normal",
            "letter_spacing": "normal",
            "case": "none",
            "wrap": "pretty",
            "text_color": "",
            "background": false,
            "background_color": "#00000026",
            "corner_radius": 0,
            "padding-block-start": 0,
            "padding-block-end": 0,
            "padding-inline-start": 0,
            "padding-inline-end": 0
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "accordion_fQYEVg": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "name": "t:names.accordion",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "caret",
            "dividers": true,
            "divider_color": "",
            "type_preset": "h5",
            "background_color": "",
            "text_color": "",
            "border": "none",
            "border_width": 1,
            "border_opacity": 100,
            "border_color": "",
            "border_radius": 0,
            "padding-block-start": 0,
            "padding-block-end": 0,
            "padding-inline-start": 0,
            "padding-inline-end": 0
          },
          "blocks": {
            "accordion_row_KUkrXJ": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Theobromin",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_8D3cqB": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Kakao ist das einzige Lebensmittel mit nennenswerten Mengen Theobromin. Eine Portion 75-prozentiger dunkler Schokolade enthält siebenmal mehr Theobromin als industrielle Milchschokolade, 17-mal mehr als Yerba Mate und 78-mal mehr als Tee. Anders als Koffein stört Theobromin den Schlaf nicht – eine große US-Studie (Grandner et al., n = 5.587) fand sogar, dass Theobromin von allen Nahrungsbestandteilen am stärksten mit der Schlafdauer zusammenhing.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_8D3cqB"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_c9CtYN": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Theophyllin",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_FqxxQK": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Ein weiteres Methylxanthin, in geringerer Konzentration. Es erhöht vor allem die Konzentrationsfähigkeit. Die Flavanole des Kakaos wirken zudem entzündungshemmend.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_FqxxQK"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_z3gX3J": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Phenylethylamin (PEA)",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_e4PkzD": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Eine Verbindung, die auch im menschlichen Gehirn vorkommt. Sie löst die Freisetzung von Endorphinen aus und regt die Produktion von Dopamin und Serotonin an – deshalb heißt sie „Liebesdroge“.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_e4PkzD"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_AJq68p": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Anandamid",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_D8arRk": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Das „Glücksmolekül“: Es aktiviert die Cannabinoidrezeptoren im Gehirn und steigert Motivation und Wohlgefühl.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_D8arRk"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_epdU7N": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Koffein",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_9HtDHA": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>In sehr geringen Mengen enthalten – nicht vergleichbar mit Kaffee, ohne Nervosität und ohne Absturz. Das Verhältnis von Theobromin zu Koffein liegt in dunkler Schokolade zwischen 7 und 16, bei Yerba Mate bei 0,4, bei Tee bei 0,1.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_9HtDHA"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_7bM3By": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Die CoCoA-Studie",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_BxMKiV": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Die randomisierte, kontrollierte Cocoa, Cognition, and Aging -Studie zeigte, dass der Verzehr von Kakaoflavanolen kognitive Funktionen, Blutdruckkontrolle und Stoffwechselprofil bei älteren Menschen verbessert.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "",
